[Event "Trompowsky Attack"]
[Opening "Trompowsky Attack"]
[ECO "A45"]
[Origin "Octávio Trompowsky (1930s)"]
[Side "white"]
[Tags "d4,offbeat"]
[Difficulty "2"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. Bg5 { The Trompowsky: White threatens to double Black's pawns with Bxf6. }
2... Ne4 { [%name 2...Ne4] The knight sidesteps and hits the bishop. }
( 2... e6 { [%name 2...e6] }
  3. e4 h6 4. Bxf6 Qxf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Qd2 { White has a big centre in return for the bishop pair. } )
( 2... d5 { [%name 2...d5] }
  3. Bxf6 exf6 4. e3 Bd6 5. c4 dxc4 6. Bxc4 O-O 7. Nc3 { Black's doubled f-pawns limit the bishop pair; White plays in the centre. } )
( 2... c5 { [%name 2...c5] }
  3. Bxf6 gxf6 4. d5 Qb6 5. Qc1 { Defending b2 while keeping the queen flexible. }
  5... f5 6. c4 )
3. Bf4 c5 4. f3 { Kicking the knight; White will build a centre with e4. }
4... Qa5+ 5. c3 Nf6 6. Nd2 { Defending against ...Qxc3 tricks and preparing e4. }
6... cxd4 7. Nb3 Qb6 8. cxd4 { White has a strong centre; Black's queen is slightly exposed. } *
